  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "37143870",
      "title": "Three Trees: Widget Tree, Element Tree & Render Tree",
      "lectureOrder": 146,
      "videoOrder": 134,
      "sourceHash": "5ee5b23f81ba82ba73284738a84a7b24f09869ae1f21977a3c7185ebabfaa39b",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.04,
          "end": 3.27,
          "en": "So let's get started.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.27,
          "end": 6.24,
          "en": "And before we have that look at keys,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.24,
          "end": 9.54,
          "en": "let's have a look at trees first.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.54,
          "end": 11.79,
          "en": "Because when working with Flutter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.79,
          "end": 15.27,
          "en": "you are essentially working with three trees,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.27,
          "end": 19.68,
          "en": "though two of those three trees are typically invisible",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.68,
          "end": 21.69,
          "en": "to you as a developer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.69,
          "end": 24,
          "en": "You do, of course, know the widget tree,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24,
          "end": 25.14,
          "en": "which you're building.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 25.14,
          "end": 26.55,
          "en": "When building a Flutter app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 26.55,
          "end": 28.02,
          "en": "you're dealing with widgets,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 28.02,
          "end": 30.24,
          "en": "and it's this combination of widgets,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 30.24,
          "end": 33.03,
          "en": "this nesting of widgets into each other,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 33.03,
          "end": 36.96,
          "en": "which we typically call a widget tree.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 36.96,
          "end": 41.04,
          "en": "But Flutter also knows a so-called element tree",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 41.04,
          "end": 43.05,
          "en": "and a render tree,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 43.05,
          "end": 46.98,
          "en": "and it helps to understand what these trees are all about",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 46.98,
          "end": 48.663,
          "en": "and how they are related.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 49.68,
          "end": 50.513,
          "en": "Now, as mentioned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 50.513,
          "end": 54.09,
          "en": "the widget tree is simply this combination of widgets",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 54.09,
          "end": 55.17,
          "en": "in your code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 55.17,
          "end": 58.35,
          "en": "So if a Flutter developer takes a look at some Flutter code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 58.35,
          "end": 61.05,
          "en": "and sees all these widgets combined with each other",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 61.05,
          "end": 62.91,
          "en": "and nested into each other,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 62.91,
          "end": 65.76,
          "en": "they would typically call that combination",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 65.76,
          "end": 67.533,
          "en": "the so-called Widget Tree.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 68.88,
          "end": 72.3,
          "en": "But Flutter actually takes that widget tree",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 72.3,
          "end": 75.6,
          "en": "and translates it into the element tree,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 75.6,
          "end": 80.6,
          "en": "which is simply in memory representation of your widgets.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 80.73,
          "end": 83.78999999999999,
          "en": "Now, with that, I don't mean the widget objects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 83.78999999999999,
          "end": 87.39,
          "en": "that are created by instantiating the widget classes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 87.39,
          "end": 90.36,
          "en": "So your classes that extend state full",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 90.36,
          "end": 91.95,
          "en": "or state less widgets,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 91.95,
          "end": 94.08,
          "en": "but I mean additional objects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 94.08,
          "end": 97.17,
          "en": "which are connected to the widget objects though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 97.17,
          "end": 100.05,
          "en": "which are created in memory by Flutter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 100.05,
          "end": 104.19,
          "en": "And Flutter creates these extra element objects in memory",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 104.19,
          "end": 109.19,
          "en": "to be able to efficiently determine required UI updates.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 109.2,
          "end": 111.53999999999999,
          "en": "Now these element objects as mentioned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 111.53999999999999,
          "end": 113.94,
          "en": "are related to your widget objects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 113.94,
          "end": 116.94,
          "en": "For example, when a widget is first encountered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 116.94,
          "end": 120.12,
          "en": "and its build method is called for the first time,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 120.12,
          "end": 123.42,
          "en": "Flutter will thereafter create a fitting element object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 123.42,
          "end": 125.4,
          "en": "and store that in memory.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 125.4,
          "end": 128.88,
          "en": "But the build method is typically called quite frequently,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 128.88,
          "end": 131.4,
          "en": "for example, because you called set state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 131.4,
          "end": 132.78,
          "en": "in a stateful widget.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 132.78,
          "end": 135.21,
          "en": "In that case, that widgets build method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 135.21,
          "end": 136.2,
          "en": "would be called again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 136.2,
          "end": 140.28,
          "en": "and all child widgets build methods would be called again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 140.28,
          "end": 143.04,
          "en": "because Flutter needs to check that entire part",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 143.04,
          "end": 144.39,
          "en": "of the widget tree",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 144.39,
          "end": 148.74,
          "en": "to make sure that the state update is represented correctly.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 148.74,
          "end": 151.65,
          "en": "But Flutter does not necessarily recreate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 151.65,
          "end": 153.81,
          "en": "all those element objects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 153.81,
          "end": 156.9,
          "en": "Instead, it only creates new elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 156.9,
          "end": 158.7,
          "en": "if you added new widgets,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 158.7,
          "end": 161.52,
          "en": "or it removes elements from the elementary",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 161.52,
          "end": 163.32,
          "en": "if widgets were removed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 163.32,
          "end": 166.023,
          "en": "for example, because of some conditional code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 167.1,
          "end": 170.43,
          "en": "So elements are actually reused if possible.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 170.43,
          "end": 173.01,
          "en": "They are not recreated all the time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 173.01,
          "end": 174.81,
          "en": "They are created initially",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 174.81,
          "end": 178.11,
          "en": "when a widgets build method is called for the first time,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 178.11,
          "end": 181.05,
          "en": "but for subsequent cause of a widget's build method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 181.05,
          "end": 183.45,
          "en": "elements are instead reused.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 183.45,
          "end": 185.91,
          "en": "But it's this element tree that's then used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 185.91,
          "end": 189.51,
          "en": "to determine which UI should actually be rendered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 189.51,
          "end": 190.68,
          "en": "on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 190.68,
          "end": 193.29,
          "en": "And that's where the render tree comes into play,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 193.29,
          "end": 195.72,
          "en": "because the render tree is the combination",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 195.72,
          "end": 198.21,
          "en": "of visible UI building blocks,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 198.21,
          "end": 200.85,
          "en": "so the things you can see on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 200.85,
          "end": 202.86,
          "en": "And creating that render tree",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 202.86,
          "end": 206.01,
          "en": "and updating the UI and the render tree, therefore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 206.01,
          "end": 208.35,
          "en": "actually takes quite a lot of work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 208.35,
          "end": 210.81,
          "en": "It has quite a big performance impact,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 210.81,
          "end": 213.78,
          "en": "and therefore, Flutter is built such that it really tries",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 213.78,
          "end": 215.97,
          "en": "to avoid touching that render tree,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 215.97,
          "end": 219.12,
          "en": "and it only re-renders parts of the UI",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 219.12,
          "end": 221.25,
          "en": "when UI updates are needed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 221.25,
          "end": 222.96,
          "en": "And if an update is needed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 222.96,
          "end": 225.87,
          "en": "is determined with help of that element tree.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 225.87,
          "end": 226.74,
          "en": "Because in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 226.74,
          "end": 230.67000000000002,
          "en": "you can think of this UI updating process like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 230.67000000000002,
          "end": 232.47,
          "en": "When the build method is called,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 232.47,
          "end": 234.75,
          "en": "Flutter checks the element tree",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 234.75,
          "end": 237.69,
          "en": "and reuses existing elements as needed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 237.69,
          "end": 241.08,
          "en": "and then thereafter, it compares the new element tree",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 241.08,
          "end": 243.12,
          "en": "to the old element tree.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 243.12,
          "end": 245.04,
          "en": "And if there are any differences,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 245.04,
          "end": 248.34,
          "en": "those differences are applied to the render tree",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 248.34,
          "end": 250.77,
          "en": "and the UI is updated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 250.77,
          "end": 254.4,
          "en": "But of course, Flutter will not re-render the entire screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 254.4,
          "end": 257.79,
          "en": "just because one tiny part of it needs to be updated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 257.79,
          "end": 259.2,
          "en": "Instead, it really takes care",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 259.2,
          "end": 261.72,
          "en": "to only partially update the UI",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 261.72,
          "end": 264.87,
          "en": "and re-render the parts that need updating.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 264.87,
          "end": 266.01,
          "en": "Now, as a developer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 266.01,
          "end": 269.22,
          "en": "you don't need to worry about the element and render tree,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 269.22,
          "end": 271.62,
          "en": "Flutter manages those trees for you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 271.62,
          "end": 274.08,
          "en": "You build your widgets with their build methods,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 274.08,
          "end": 275.19,
          "en": "and that's it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 275.19,
          "end": 276.12,
          "en": "But as a developer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 276.12,
          "end": 278.82,
          "en": "you should always also understand",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 278.82,
          "end": 280.62,
          "en": "what's happening behind the scenes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 280.62,
          "end": 282.78,
          "en": "and therefore, this year is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 282.78,
          "end": 284.553,
          "en": "what's happening behind the scenes.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
